{% else %}

CONTENT: No data supplied - invent realistic, specific figures and text.
Real-sounding numbers ($42.8M, 114%, +18% QoQ), named entities, concise prose.
Never "XX%", "TBD", "Lorem ipsum", "Company A", "Metric 1". Every value should
look like it came from a real business report.
{% endif %}

{% if band_heights %}
HEIGHT BUDGET — PRE-COMPUTED (use these exact pixel heights):
Each component above marked with → h="NNN" has a pre-computed band height.
Copy that h value EXACTLY onto the component's container (VStack/HStack/Chart/Table).
Do NOT recalculate or adjust these heights — they are already budgeted to fit
within 720px with padding={{ band_heights.get('_padding', 48) }} and gap={{ band_heights.get('_gap', 24) }}.
Use padding="48" and gap="24" on the root VStack unless you have a specific reason not to.
{% else %}
HEIGHT BUDGET — MANDATORY ARITHMETIC before writing any XML:
1. Pick padding P and gap G for the root VStack.
2. Header band has no h (auto, ~80-90).
3. Compute available_h = 720 - 2*P - header_h_est - (N_bands-1)*G.
4. Assign each content band an explicit h from its weight tag.
5. ADD UP: header_est + all band h values + all gaps + 2*P. The total MUST be <= 700.
   If over 700, SHRINK the largest band or drop a minor band. NEVER exceed 720.
6. Untagged components are peers (equal split).
{% endif %}
Do NOT use <Layer> for content layouts — Layer children stack on top of each
other causing overlaps. Use VStack/HStack flow layouts. Reserve Layer ONLY for
intentional overlays (watermarks, background decorations behind content).

Output the POM XML for this slide - a single <Slide> element, no <Theme>, no
markdown fences, no commentary.
